His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan in Council may make rules for the purposes of this Act, and without prejudice to the generality of the foregoing, may in particular make rules for —

(a) prescribing the fees to be charged under this Act;

(b) prescribing the manner in which the Registrars shall exercise the powers conferred on them by this Act;

(c) providing for the safe custody of all registers and Registrar’s Notebooks kept under this Act and all declarations made for the purposes of this Act; and

(d) generally for carrying out the purposes of this Act. Dissolution of marriages
